  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Incubate, Accelerate, Thrive (IAT-SL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Incubate, Accelerate, Thrive (IAT-SL) will strengthen Sierra Leone&#xbf;s innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystem by supporting a select group of well-performing incubators and accelerators to deliver sustainable, high-quality business support services. Organisations such as Innovation SL (Orange Corners), E-Women Makeni, EnRICH Hub and others play a pivotal role in nurturing start-ups, yet many face challenges linked to financial sustainability, operational capacity, digital infrastructure and limited ability to scale. Support is often short-term and fragmented, reducing continuity and long-term impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Under Outcome 1 of the BEC4S Programme, the European Union will provide strategic grants to 3&#xbf;4 incubators selected through a competitive process, complemented by targeted technical assistance. This approach strengthens institutional resilience, reduces administrative fragmentation and reinforces incubators as core actors for MSME growth and job creation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The action focuses on three result areas:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Strengthened Institutional Capacity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Grants for operational strengthening, digital upgrades and governance improvement&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Technical assistance in management, sustainability planning and monitoring &amp; evaluation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Support for coordination and knowledge-sharing under MTI/SMEDA oversight&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. High-Quality and Inclusive Entrepreneurship Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Standardised incubation and acceleration curricula integrating digitalisation and green innovation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Improved mentoring, peer learning and digital tools&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Increased participation of women and youth, including outside Freetown&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Promotion of circular economy, renewable energy, agritech and digital solutions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Improved Access to Markets, Finance and Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Partnerships with banks, MFIs, impact investors and private firms&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Investor pitch sessions, innovation fairs and B2B matchmaking&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &#xbf; Support to pilot projects addressing local economic and sustainability challenges&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Expected results include stronger, financially resilient incubators; increased opportunities for start-ups to scale; enhanced market access and financing opportunities; and expanded participation of young and women entrepreneurs in innovation-driven sectors. The initiative contributes directly to BEC4S Outcome 1 and Output 1.3 by strengthening business support systems and advancing digital and green innovation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;IAT-SL aligns with Global Gateway and NDICI&#xbf;Global Europe priorities on competitiveness, sustainability, digital transformation and inclusive economic empowerment. Coordination will ensure complementarity with UNDP, UNIDO, GIZ, the World Bank, Invest Salone and Orange Corners. Sustainability will be promoted through diversified revenue models, strengthened management systems and durable public-private partnerships, helping establish a more coherent and impactful innovation ecosystem in Sierra Leone.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
